    <main class="p-admissions-information-contact-index" data-page-admissions-information-contact-index="root">
        <div class="c-sectionKv" data-section-kv="root">
            <div class="c-sectionKv-container">
                <div class="c-sectionKv-inner">
                    <h1 class="c-h1"><span class="c-h1-text" data-text-gradient-peek-by-scroll="root"><span class="c-textGradientPeek" data-text-gradient-peek="root">Language requirements</span></span></h1>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="p-admissions-information-contact-index-contents p-fixed-page-contents" data-page-admissions-information-contact-index="content" data-page="content">
            <section class="c-blockSection is-bg">
                <div class="c-blockSection-inner">
                    <div class="inner-s">

<p>Nagoya University offers flexible language options for international students, with programs available in both English and Japanese depending on your academic goals.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">English language requirements</h2>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">G30 International Programs (taught entirely in English)</h3>



<p>For undergraduate and graduate degree programs taught entirely in English:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>English proficiency test is required</strong> for most applicants</li>



<li><strong>Exemption is available</strong> for students who completed four or more consecutive years of secondary education where English was the primary language of instruction</li>



<li><strong>Accepted tests include:</strong>
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>TOEFL</li>



<li>IELTS</li>



<li>Duolingo English Test</li>
</ul>
</li>



<li><strong>No Japanese proficiency is required</strong> for admission to these programs</li>
</ul>



<p><a href="https://admissions.g30.nagoya-u.ac.jp/admissions/undergraduate/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Learn more about G30 International Programs</a></p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Exchange programs (NUPACE)</h3>



<p>For exchange students participating in the Nagoya University Program for Academic Exchange:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>No Japanese language requirement</strong> to participate</li>



<li><strong>English proficiency requirement</strong> for non-native English speakers:
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>TOEFL: 550 (CBT=213; iBT=79)</li>



<li>TOEIC: 730</li>



<li>IELTS: overall band score of 5.5</li>



<li>Or equivalent scores</li>
</ul>
</li>



<li><strong>Exemption available </strong>for students studying full-time at universities where English is the medium of instruction</li>
</ul>



<p><a href="https://nupace.iee.nagoya-u.ac.jp/en/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Learn more about NUPACE Programs</a></p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Japanese language requirements</h2>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Regular Japanese-taught programs</h3>



<p>For students who want to take regular university courses taught in Japanese:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>JLPT N1 level required</strong> (Japanese Language Proficiency Test level 1)</li>



<li>Alternative equivalent qualifications may be accepted</li>
</ul>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Specialized programs</h3>



<p><strong>Intensive Programme in Advanced Japanese:</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>JLPT N2 level minimum</strong> required for enrollment</li>
</ul>



<p><strong>NUPACE exchange students:</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Students with <strong>JLPT N1</strong> may register for regular Japanese-taught courses</li>



<li>Core NUPACE curriculum taught primarily in English</li>
</ul>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Program flexibility</h2>



<p>Nagoya University provides multiple pathways for international students:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Full degree programs</strong> available entirely in English through G30 International Programs</li>



<li><strong>Exchange opportunities</strong> with minimal language barriers through NUPACE</li>



<li><strong>Japanese language support</strong> through comprehensive language programs</li>



<li><strong>Mixed approach</strong>  allowing qualified students to combine English and Japanese-taught courses<br></li>
</ul>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Additional resources</h2>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><a href="https://admissions.g30.nagoya-u.ac.jp/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Nagoya University International Programs</a></li>



<li><a href="https://en.nagoya-u.ac.jp/admissions/">Nagoya University main admissions page</a></li>



<li><a href="https://www.jlpt.jp/e/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Japanese Language Proficiency Test (JLPT) information</a></li>
</ul>



<p>For the most current requirements and specific program details, please check the <a href="https://en.nagoya-u.ac.jp/admissions/">admissions program pages</a> or contact the university directly.</p>



<p></p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            
        </div>
